# Next.js - Modern App Router Patterns & Best Practices

**Status:** ✅ Core Feature - Next.js (App Router, Server Components, RSC)

This document defines Spark's approach to Next.js component generation, focusing on modern App Router patterns, Server Components, and Next.js 13+ best practices.

## Philosophy: Server-First, Progressive Enhancement

**Core Principles:**
1. **Server Components by Default** - Use React Server Components (RSC) unless client interactivity needed
2. **Progressive Enhancement** - Build with Server Components, add Client Components only when necessary
3. **App Router First** - Default to App Router (13+), support Pages Router when detected
4. **Performance Focused** - Leverage Next.js optimizations (Image, Font, Metadata)
5. **Type Safety** - TypeScript with strict mode enabled

## Next.js Project Detection

### Detection Patterns

```javascript
const detectNextJS = () => {
  const patterns = {
    // Next.js App Router (13+)
    appRouter: {
      indicators: [
        'app/ directory exists',
        'app/layout.tsx or app/layout.js',
        'next.config.js with appDir',
        'package.json with next@13 or higher'
      ],
      structure: {
        components: 'components/',
        serverComponents: 'components/server/',
        clientComponents: 'components/client/',
        uiComponents: 'components/ui/',
        app: 'app/'
      },
      features: {
        serverComponents: true,
        serverActions: true,
        streaming: true,
        suspense: true
      }
    },
    
    // Next.js Pages Router (12 and earlier)
    pagesRouter: {
      indicators: [
        'pages/ directory exists',
        'pages/_app.tsx or pages/_app.js',
        'pages/api/ directory'
      ],
      structure: {
        components: 'components/',
        pages: 'pages/',
        api: 'pages/api/',
        public: 'public/'
      },
      features: {
        serverComponents: false,
        getServerSideProps: true,
        getStaticProps: true,
        apiRoutes: true
      }
    },
    
    // Common Next.js Patterns
    common: {
      typescript: 'tsconfig.json exists',
      tailwind: 'tailwind.config.js or tailwind.config.ts',
      srcDirectory: 'src/ directory exists',
      publicDirectory: 'public/ directory exists'
    }
  };
  
  return analyzeAndRecommend(patterns);
};
```

